this command give you token so you must to go:
To add a TXT record in ArvanCloud DNS, do this:

✅ Steps (ArvanCloud Panel)

Log in to ArvanCloud panel

Go to DNS section

Select your domain

Open the Records (رکوردها) tab

Click Add record (افزودن رکورد)

Set the fields like this:

Type: TXT

Name / Host:

Use @ → for root domain (example.com)

Use _acme-challenge → for SSL validation

Use something like google._domainkey → for email/DKIM

Value / Content:

Paste the TXT value exactly (no quotes unless Arvan adds them automatically)

TTL:

Default (Auto or 300 seconds is fine)

Click Save ✅


For this host:

_acme-challenge.saller.beroztest.ir

✅ What to enter in ArvanCloud TXT record

In ArvanCloud you must NOT enter the full domain.
You only enter the relative name.

Correct configuration:

Type: TXT

Name (Host):

_acme-challenge.saller


Value (Content):

<token provided by certbot / acme.sh>


TTL: Default / Auto

ArvanCloud will automatically append the domain, resulting in:

_acme-challenge.saller.beroztest.ir

❌ Common mistake

Do NOT put this in the Name field:

_acme-challenge.saller.beroztest.ir


That would create:

_acme-challenge.saller.beroztest.ir.beroztest.ir


…and SSL verification will fail.

✅ Verify the TXT record

After saving (wait 1–5 minutes), check with:

dig TXT _acme-challenge.saller.beroztest.ir


You should see the exact token returned.

NOTE: if you set this *.berooztest.ir  you can give ssh for all domain
